---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="Getting Started with SoloMD — Install, Open a Folder, View Modes, Updates & Encrypted Sync"
  description="Install SoloMD on macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, or Android, open your first folder, switch between Live, Source, Split, and Preview modes, and keep your notes safe."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container docs-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/docs/">Docs</a> / <span>Getting Started</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>Getting Started</h1>
      <p class="lead">From download to your first saved note, in about three minutes.</p>

      <h2>1. Install &amp; One-Click Updates</h2>
      <table class="kb-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>How to install</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>macOS</th><td><code>brew install --cask zhitongblog/solomd/solomd</code>, or download the signed &amp; notarized universal <code>.dmg</code> from <a href="/">solomd.app</a> and drag to Applications (Apple Silicon &amp; Intel, macOS 10.15+).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Windows</th><td>Download the <code>.msi</code> (x64 or arm64) or the no-install <code>-portable.zip</code> (create a <code>data/</code> folder next to <code>SoloMD.exe</code> for portable settings). Includes a Windows Explorer “New → Markdown Document” shell entry.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Linux</th><td><code>.AppImage</code>, <code>.deb</code>, or <code>.rpm</code> (x64 and arm64), using <code>xdg-portal</code> native file dialogs for smooth KDE Plasma / GNOME Wayland compatibility (<a href="/docs/linux/">distro guide</a>).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>iOS / iPadOS / Android</th><td>iOS 15+ on the App Store (edits Files-app notes in place); Android 7+ signed APK (with SAF folder access and foldable support).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        <strong>In-app one-click update installer</strong>: when a new release is available, click the update button in the header or <em>Settings → About</em> to download and launch the native installer directly inside the app.
      </p>

      <h3>Windows: taskbar icon shows blank?</h3>
      <p>
        If a pinned taskbar icon appears blank after an upgrade, Windows’ icon cache is holding a stale entry. Run these four lines in Command Prompt to refresh it:
      </p>
      <pre><code>taskkill /f /im explorer.exe
del /f /q %LocalAppData%\IconCache.db
del /f /q %LocalAppData%\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer\iconcache_*.db
start explorer.exe</code></pre>

      <h2>2. Open a file or a workspace folder</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start typing right away</strong>: unsaved drafts live in memory and survive app restarts via session restore.</li>
        <li><strong>Open a single file</strong>: File → Open (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + O</kbd>), drag &amp; drop onto the window, or double-click a <code>.md</code> file. When editing a single file without a workspace open, the sidebar offers a one-click button to open its parent folder.</li>
        <li><strong>Open a folder (recommended)</strong>: File → Open Folder turns that directory into your <em>workspace</em> — enabling the file tree, full-text search, <code>#tags</code>, <code>[[backlinks]]</code>, knowledge graph, and per-workspace tab memory.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Tabs, MRU switching &amp; split panes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Drag to reorder &amp; filter open tabs</strong>: drag tabs along the strip to reorder them; when 2+ tabs are open, click the <code>⌄</code> button at the end of the tab bar to filter and jump to any open tab.</li>
        <li><strong>Two ways to cycle tabs</strong>: press <kbd>Ctrl + Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl + Shift + Tab</kbd> to cycle in <strong>Most Recently Used (MRU)</strong> order, or <kbd>⌘⇧[</kbd> / <kbd>⌘⇧]</kbd> (<kbd>Ctrl + PageUp / PageDown</kbd>) to move in visual tab bar order.</li>
        <li><strong>Split panes</strong>: press <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + \</kbd> (or drag a tab onto the editor) to view two notes side by side, and close any split pane with its corner close button.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Four view modes, one click apart</h2>
      <p>Switch modes from the quiet header pill or with shortcuts — your exact viewport scroll offset and cursor position are preserved across modes:</p>
      <table class="kb-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Shortcut</th><th>What you see</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Live Edit</th><td><kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + /</kbd></td><td>Default WYSIWYG mode: formatting, tables, math, Mermaid, images, and callouts render in place; the caret line reveals raw Markdown.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Source</th><td><kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + /</kbd></td><td>Raw Markdown source with syntax highlighting.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Split</th><td><kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + P</kbd></td><td>Source on the left, rendered preview on the right, scroll-synced with a draggable divider.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Preview</th><td><kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + V</kbd></td><td>Clean reading view with per-tab scroll memory, plus presentation Slideshow mode (with light/dark theme toggle <kbd>T</kbd> and text zoom).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>5. Next steps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/editor/">Editor deep-dive</a> — two-stage code block Select All, indented code fences in lists, Excel table paste, auto-numbered headings.</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/sync/">Sync, history &amp; encrypted cloud backup</a> — WebDAV E2EE, Local Cloud Drive Encrypted Vault, Direct Cloud OpenAPI, and GitHub sync.</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/shortcuts/">Keyboard shortcuts</a> — all 60+ shortcuts and the Typora / Word Writer preset.</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/export/">Export &amp; Copy</a> — vector PDF, native DOCX, Copy as Word, and Rich HTML copy.</li>
      </ul>

      <Giscus />
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
